      "description": "Watch Strasbourg vs Lens highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. On August 29, 2026 , Strasbourg and Lens faced off in a high-stakes Ligue 1 encounter where the drama shifted with every whistle. This clash under the lights promised tension and tactical battles from the very start, as both sides sought to climb the early-season table. Thauvin Breaks the Deadlock The match began with Strasbourg trying to establish dominance, with Giovanni Reyna seeing an early effort blocked. However, the momentum swung toward the visitors in the 36th minute. Jeyland Mitchell was penalized for tripping Abdallah Sima inside the box, earning a yellow card and handing Lens a golden opportunity. Florian Thauvin stepped up to the spot and coolly converted with his left foot, sending Filip Joergensen the wrong way to give Lens a 1-0 lead at the 38-minute mark. Lens looked to consolidate their lead as the first half drew to a close, but Strasbourg remained a persistent threat. The home side struggled to find the final ball, with offside flags and resolute defending from the likes of Matthieu Udol keeping them at bay until the interval. The Yassine Show and VAR Drama The second half saw Strasbourg emerge with renewed energy, and they didn't have to wait long for an equalizer. In the 48th minute, Gessime Yassine found the back of the net with a clinical right-footed finish following an assist from Sebastian Nanasi . The home side thought they had taken the lead ten minutes later when Nanasi headed home, but a lengthy VAR review eventually revoked the goal for offside, keeping the scores level. The final ten minutes were filled with controversy and brilliance. In the 84th minute, Yassine was booked for simulation in the penalty area, but he responded perfectly just sixty seconds later. A brilliant pass from Samuel Amo-Ameyaw set up Yassine , who struck a superb volley into the net. After another tense VAR check, the goal was confirmed in the 86th minute, sparking wild celebrations among the home support. Lens Push for a Late Equalizer As the match entered eight minutes of stoppage time, Lens threw everything forward. Florian Thauvin continued to deliver dangerous corners, and Florian Sotoca nearly snatched a point in the 98th minute with a powerful header. However, Filip Joergensen was well-positioned to make a comfortable save, ensuring that Strasbourg held on for a hard-fought 2-1 victory in a game defined by clinical finishing and technology-driven drama."
